  CVE-2025-50666|2026-04-08T19:24:17.250|2026-04-08T21:26:13.410|0.0|NONE|N/A|N/A|false|A buffer overflow vulnerability exists in D-Link DI-8003 16.07.26A1 due to improper handling of multiple parameters in the /web_post.asp endpoint. An attacker can exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP GET request in parameters such as name, en, user_id, log, and time.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-50666|0.00008|0.00773|0.0002
  CVE-2025-50665|2026-04-08T19:24:17.140|2026-04-08T21:26:13.410|0.0|NONE|N/A|N/A|false|A buffer overflow vulnerability exists in D-Link DI-8003 16.07.26A1 due to improper handling of input parameters in the /web_keyword.asp endpoint. An attacker can exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP GET request via the name, en, time, mem_gb2312, and mem_utf8 parameters.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-50665|0.00008|0.00773|0.0002
