  CVE-2026-35537|2026-04-03T04:17:10.313|2026-04-03T16:10:23.730|3.7|LOW|CWE-502|N/A|false|An issue was discovered in Roundcube Webmail before 1.5.14 and 1.6.14. Unsafe deserialization in the redis/memcache session handler may lead to arbitrary file write operations by unauthenticated attackers via crafted session data.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35537|0.00040|0.12104|2.5912
  CVE-2026-35536|2026-04-03T04:16:53.550|2026-04-03T16:10:23.730|7.2|HIGH|CWE-159|N/A|false|In Tornado before 6.5.5, cookie attribute injection could occur because the domain, path, and samesite arguments to .RequestHandler.set_cookie were not checked for crafted characters.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35536|0.00048|0.15021|5.0414
  CVE-2026-35535|2026-04-03T03:16:18.233|2026-04-03T16:10:23.730|7.4|HIGH|CWE-271|N/A|false|In Sudo through 1.9.17p2 before 3e474c2, a failure of a setuid, setgid, or setgroups call, during a privilege drop before running the mailer, is not a fatal error and can lead to privilege escalation.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-35535|0.00005|0.00277|5.1801
  CVE-2026-28815|2026-04-03T03:16:18.093|2026-04-03T16:10:23.730|7.5|HIGH|CWE-125|N/A|false|A remote attacker can supply a short X-Wing HPKE encapsulated key and trigger an out-of-bounds read in the C decapsulation path, potentially causing a crash or memory disclosure depending on runtime protections. This issue is fixed in swift-crypto version 4.3.1.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-28815|0.00045|0.13932|5.2514
